From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfaacenc, winegstreamer: The AAC encoder MFT (9400)

Wine had no audio encoder MFT at all (only H.264): NAudio's MediaFoundationEncoder
(MFTranscodeGetAudioOutputAvailableTypes and a sink writer to .m4a/.mp4), screen recorders writing
H.264 + AAC .mp4 files and transcoders found none. CLSID_AACMFTEncoder (mfaacenc.dll, as on Windows)
as Microsoft documents it: AAC-LC from 16-bit PCM, mono/stereo/5.1, 44.1/48 kHz, at
12000/16000/20000/24000 bytes/s (x6 for 5.1), raw or ADTS frames of 1024 samples, the HEAACWAVEINFO tail
and AudioSpecificConfig in MF_MT_USER_DATA, types in either order, MF_E_NO_SAMPLE_TIMESTAMP/DURATION.
Encoding through wg_transform (GStreamer's libav AAC encoder); the AudioSpecificConfig, ADTS headers
and sample times are the transform's own.
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/aac_encoder.c
@@ -0,0 +1,823 @@
